Plate tectonics (from Latin tectonicus, from Ancient Greek τεκτονικός (tektonikós) ''pertaining to building'') is the scientific theory that Earth''s lithosphere comprises a number of large tectonic plates, which have been slowly moving since 3–4 billion years ago. The model builds on the concept of continental drift, an idea developed during the first decades of the 20th century.

Text 2
A volcano is a vent or fissure in the crust of a planetary-mass object that allows hot lava, volcanic ash, and gases to escape from a magma chamber below the surface. On Earth, volcanoes are most often found where tectonic plates are diverging or converging, and because most of Earth''s plate boundaries are underwater, most volcanoes are found underwater.', 'Which choice best describes the relationship between the two texts?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "Text 2 traces the history of the theory presented in Text 1."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Text 2 describes a surface phenomenon that occurs at the plate boundaries introduced in Text 1."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Text 2 refutes the theory presented in Text 1."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Text 2 argues that volcanoes are unrelated to geology."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Plate tectonics", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plate_tectonics; Wikipedia, "Volcano", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volcano', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M37-X002', 'B', ARRAY['B']::TEXT[], 'Text 1 introduces the theory of moving tectonic plates. Text 2 then explains where volcanoes occur, locating most of them at the diverging or converging boundaries of those plates, so it describes a phenomenon produced at the boundaries Text 1 identifies.', '{"C": "Text 2 accepts and uses plate boundaries.", "A": "Text 2 describes volcanoes, not the theory''s history.", "D": "Text 2 explains volcanoes through plate movement."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, external_id, assessments, section, domain, skill, difficulty, format, stimulus, prompt, choices, figure_metadata, source_id, source_name, license, attribution, is_released_practice_set, status) VALUES ('RW-M37-X003', 'HDSAT-RW-M37-X003', ARRAY['SAT', 'PSAT/NMSQT', 'PSAT 10', 'PSAT 8/9']::TEXT[], 'Reading and Writing', 'Craft and Structure', 'Cross-Text Connections', 'Easy', 'multiple_choice', 'Text 1
The Solar System is the gravitationally bound system of the Sun and the masses that orbit it, most prominently its eight planets, of which Earth is one. The Solar System is an isolated single-star planetary system (not part of a larger star system) within the Milky Way Galaxy.

Text 2
An exoplanet or extrasolar planet is a planet outside the Solar System. The first confirmed detection of an exoplanet was in 1992 around a pulsar, and the first detection around a main-sequence star was in 1995.', 'Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the argument in Text 1?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "By arguing that the Sun is not part of the Solar System."}, {"id": "B", "text": "By extending the discussion beyond the single-star system described in Text 1 to planets that orbit other stars."}, {"id": "C", "text": "By denying that the Solar System contains eight planets."}, {"id": "D", "text": "By claiming that no planets exist outside the Solar System."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Solar System", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solar_System; Wikipedia, "Exoplanet", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exoplanet', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
