The American Civil War (April 12, 1861 – May 26, 1865; also known by other names) was a civil war in the United States between the Union ("the North") and the Confederacy ("the South"), which was formed in 1861 by Southern states that had seceded from the Union to preserve slavery in the United States. The South saw slavery as threatened because of the election of Abraham Lincoln as president in 1860 and the growing abolitionist movement in the North.

Text 2
The Reconstruction era, often simply called Reconstruction, was a period in United States history that followed the American Civil War (1861–1865) and was dominated by the legal, social, and political challenges of the abolition of slavery and federal control over, and reintegration of, the former Confederate States into the United States. Three amendments were added to the United States Constitution to grant citizenship and equal civil rights to the newly freed slaves.', 'Which choice best describes the relationship between the two texts?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "Text 2 describes the political aftermath of the conflict described in Text 1."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Text 2 compares the war with a later conflict."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Text 2 offers a cause of the war described in Text 1."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Text 2 disputes the outcome of the war."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "American Civil War", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Civil_War; Wikipedia, "Reconstruction era", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reconstruction_era', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M37-X008', 'A', ARRAY['A']::TEXT[], 'Text 1 narrates the Civil War and its origins in the conflict over slavery. Text 2 begins after the war and describes Reconstruction''s legal and political tasks, so it supplies the aftermath of the conflict Text 1 describes.', '{"C": "Text 2 is set after the war, not before it.", "D": "Text 2 accepts the war''s outcome and addresses its consequences.", "B": "Text 2 discusses Reconstruction, not another war."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, external_id, assessments, section, domain, skill, difficulty, format, stimulus, prompt, choices, figure_metadata, source_id, source_name, license, attribution, is_released_practice_set, status) VALUES ('RW-M37-X009', 'HDSAT-RW-M37-X009', ARRAY['SAT', 'PSAT/NMSQT', 'PSAT 10', 'PSAT 8/9']::TEXT[], 'Reading and Writing', 'Craft and Structure', 'Cross-Text Connections', 'Hard', 'multiple_choice', 'Text 1
In microeconomics, supply and demand is an economic model of price determination in a market. It postulates that, holding all else equal, the unit price for a particular good or other traded item in a perfectly competitive market, will vary until it settles at the market-clearing price, where the quantity demanded equals the quantity supplied such that an economic equilibrium is achieved for price and quantity transacted.

Text 2
In economics, inflation is an increase in the average price of goods and services in terms of money, though it originally referred to the increase of the money supply (monetary inflation) that can cause such a universal shift. This increase is measured using a price index, typically a consumer price index (CPI).', 'Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the argument in Text 1?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "By claiming that inflation has nothing to do with prices."}, {"id": "B", "text": "By shifting from the price of a single good in one market to the economy-wide average price level."}, {"id": "C", "text": "By arguing that market equilibrium is impossible."}, {"id": "D", "text": "By denying that prices are determined by supply and demand."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Supply and demand", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supply_and_demand; Wikipedia, "Inflation", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inflation', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M37-X009', 'B', ARRAY['B']::TEXT[], 'Text 1 models how supply and demand set the price of a particular good in a competitive market. Text 2 discusses inflation as a rise in the average price of goods and services, measured by a price index, so its author would move from one market to the economy-wide price level.', '{"D": "Text 2 does not reject price determination.", "A": "Inflation is defined as a rise in average prices.", "C": "Text 2 does not dispute equilibrium."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
