In microeconomics, supply and demand is an economic model of price determination in a market. It postulates that, holding all else equal, the unit price for a particular good or other traded item in a perfectly competitive market, will vary until it settles at the market-clearing price, where the quantity demanded equals the quantity supplied such that an economic equilibrium is achieved for price and quantity transacted.

Text 2
In economics, inflation is an increase in the average price of goods and services in terms of money, though it originally referred to the increase of the money supply (monetary inflation) that can cause such a universal shift. This increase is measured using a price index, typically a consumer price index (CPI).', 'Which choice best describes the relationship between the two texts?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "Text 2 rejects the idea of market-clearing prices."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Text 2 moves from a single-market model to a measure of prices across the economy."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Text 2 applies the model in Text 1 to a single firm."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Text 2 describes the history of money rather than prices."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Supply and demand", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supply_and_demand; Wikipedia, "Inflation", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inflation', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M37-X010', 'B', ARRAY['B']::TEXT[], 'Text 1 presents a microeconomic model of price in one competitive market. Text 2 defines inflation in terms of the average price of goods and services and a price index, so it shifts the scale from a single market to the whole economy.', '{"C": "Text 2 discusses average prices, not one firm.", "A": "Text 2 does not address market clearing.", "D": "Text 2 is about price levels and measurement."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
