Sign languages (also known as signed languages) are languages that use the visual-manual modality to convey meaning rather than spoken words. They are expressed through manual articulation in combination with non-manual markers, and are full-fledged natural languages with their own grammar and lexicon.', 'Which choice best describes the relationship between the two texts?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "Text 2 claims that sign languages lack a lexicon."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Text 2 describes how children acquire spoken words."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Text 2 describes a visual-manual kind of language that the general capacity in Text 1 would include."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Text 2 argues that language acquisition is impossible."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Language acquisition", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Language_acquisition; Wikipedia, "Sign language", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sign_language', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M37-X012', 'C', ARRAY['C']::TEXT[], 'Text 1 describes the general human capacity to acquire language. Text 2 characterizes sign languages as full natural languages conveyed through a visual-manual modality, so it presents a kind of language that the capacity in Text 1 would encompass.', '{"D": "Text 2 treats sign languages as learnable natural languages.", "B": "Text 2 is about signed, not spoken, language.", "A": "Text 2 says sign languages have their own lexicon."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, external_id, assessments, section, domain, skill, difficulty, format, stimulus, prompt, choices, figure_metadata, source_id, source_name, license, attribution, is_released_practice_set, status) VALUES ('RW-M37-X013', 'HDSAT-RW-M37-X013', ARRAY['SAT', 'PSAT/NMSQT', 'PSAT 10', 'PSAT 8/9']::TEXT[], 'Reading and Writing', 'Craft and Structure', 'Cross-Text Connections', 'Medium', 'multiple_choice', 'Text 1
A glacier forms where the accumulation of snow exceeds its ablation over many years, often centuries.

Text 2
The water cycle (or hydrologic cycle or hydrological cycle) is a biogeochemical cycle that involves the continuous change in form of water on, above and below the surface of the Earth across different reservoirs. The mass of water on Earth remains fairly constant over time.', 'Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the argument in Text 1?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "By denying that glaciers are made of water."}, {"id": "B", "text": "By arguing that glaciers are not part of the water cycle."}, {"id": "C", "text": "By claiming that water never changes form."}, {"id": "D", "text": "By placing the ice body described in Text 1 within a global cycle of water moving among reservoirs."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Glacier", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glacier; Wikipedia, "Water cycle", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water_cycle', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M37-X013', 'D', ARRAY['D']::TEXT[], 'Text 1 explains that a glacier forms where snow accumulation exceeds ablation. Text 2 describes water continuously changing form across reservoirs, so its author would place glaciers within that global cycle.', '{"A": "Text 2 is about water in all its forms.", "C": "Text 2 says water continuously changes form.", "B": "Glaciers are one of the reservoirs Text 2 implies."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
