A glacier forms where the accumulation of snow exceeds its ablation over many years, often centuries.

Text 2
The water cycle (or hydrologic cycle or hydrological cycle) is a biogeochemical cycle that involves the continuous change in form of water on, above and below the surface of the Earth across different reservoirs. The mass of water on Earth remains fairly constant over time.', 'Which choice best describes the relationship between the two texts?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "Text 2 explains how glaciers carve landforms."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Text 2 argues that glaciers are not ice."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Text 2 traces the history of a particular glacier."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Text 2 describes the larger system in which the ice formation in Text 1 is one reservoir."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Glacier", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glacier; Wikipedia, "Water cycle", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water_cycle', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M37-X014', 'D', ARRAY['D']::TEXT[], 'Text 1 defines how a glacier forms from accumulated snow. Text 2 describes the water cycle as water changing form across reservoirs while the total mass stays constant, a larger system that includes glacial ice.', '{"A": "Landform carving is not mentioned in Text 2.", "B": "Text 2 treats ice as one form of water.", "C": "Text 2 is general, not a single glacier''s history."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, external_id, assessments, section, domain, skill, difficulty, format, stimulus, prompt, choices, figure_metadata, source_id, source_name, license, attribution, is_released_practice_set, status) VALUES ('RW-M37-X015', 'HDSAT-RW-M37-X015', ARRAY['SAT', 'PSAT/NMSQT', 'PSAT 10', 'PSAT 8/9']::TEXT[], 'Reading and Writing', 'Craft and Structure', 'Cross-Text Connections', 'Easy', 'multiple_choice', 'Text 1
A cognitive bias is a systematic pattern of deviation from the norm or rationality in judgment. Individuals create their own "subjective reality" from their perception of the input.

Text 2
Confirmation bias (also confirmatory bias, myside bias, or congeniality bias) is the tendency to search for, interpret, favor and recall information in a way that confirms or supports one''s prior beliefs, values, or decisions. People display this bias when they select information that supports their views, ignoring contrary information or when they interpret ambiguous evidence as supporting their existing attitudes.', 'Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the argument in Text 1?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "By denying that people have subjective perceptions."}, {"id": "B", "text": "By arguing that judgment is always rational."}, {"id": "C", "text": "By giving a specific example of the systematic deviation from rationality described in Text 1."}, {"id": "D", "text": "By claiming that confirmation bias is not a bias."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Cognitive bias", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cognitive_bias; Wikipedia, "Confirmation bias", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Confirmation_bias', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M37-X015', 'C', ARRAY['C']::TEXT[], 'Text 1 defines cognitive bias broadly as a systematic deviation from rational judgment. Text 2 describes confirmation bias as a specific tendency to favor information that supports prior beliefs, so its author would offer that tendency as an instance of the general pattern.', '{"A": "Text 2 describes how people select supporting information.", "D": "Text 2 names confirmation bias as a bias.", "B": "Text 2 documents departures from rational judgment."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, external_id, assessments, section, domain, skill, difficulty, format, stimulus, prompt, choices, figure_metadata, source_id, source_name, license, attribution, is_released_practice_set, status) VALUES ('RW-M37-X016', 'HDSAT-RW-M37-X016', ARRAY['SAT', 'PSAT/NMSQT', 'PSAT 10', 'PSAT 8/9']::TEXT[], 'Reading and Writing', 'Craft and Structure', 'Cross-Text Connections', 'Medium', 'multiple_choice', 'Text 1
A cognitive bias is a systematic pattern of deviation from the norm or rationality in judgment. Individuals create their own "subjective reality" from their perception of the input.

Text 2
Confirmation bias (also confirmatory bias, myside bias, or congeniality bias) is the tendency to search for, interpret, favor and recall information in a way that confirms or supports one''s prior beliefs, values, or decisions. People display this bias when they select information that supports their views, ignoring contrary information or when they interpret ambiguous evidence as supporting their existing attitudes.', 'Which choice best describes the relationship between the two texts?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "Text 2 argues that biases cannot be studied."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Text 2 describes a bias unrelated to judgment."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Text 2 rejects the definition in Text 1."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Text 2 identifies one specific form of the general pattern defined in Text 1."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Cognitive bias", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cognitive_bias; Wikipedia, "Confirmation bias", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Confirmation_bias', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M37-X016', 'D', ARRAY['D']::TEXT[], 'Text 1 offers a general definition of cognitive bias. Text 2 describes confirmation bias as a particular tendency in how people search for and interpret information, which makes it one specific form of the pattern Text 1 defines.', '{"C": "Text 2 works within the concept of bias.", "B": "Confirmation bias concerns judgment and belief.", "A": "Text 2 describes observable tendencies."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, external_id, assessments, section, domain, skill, difficulty, format, stimulus, prompt, choices, figure_metadata, source_id, source_name, license, attribution, is_released_practice_set, status) VALUES ('RW-M37-X017', 'HDSAT-RW-M37-X017', ARRAY['SAT', 'PSAT/NMSQT', 'PSAT 10', 'PSAT 8/9']::TEXT[], 'Reading and Writing', 'Craft and Structure', 'Cross-Text Connections', 'Medium', 'multiple_choice', 'Text 1
An antibiotic is a type of antimicrobial substance which is active against bacteria. It is the most important type of antibacterial agent for fighting bacterial infections, and antibiotic medications are widely used in the treatment and prevention of such infections.

Text 2
Epidemiology is the study and analysis of the distribution (who, when, and where), patterns and determinants of health and disease conditions in a defined population, and application of this knowledge to prevent diseases. It is a cornerstone of public health, and shapes policy decisions and evidence-based practice by identifying risk factors for disease and targets for preventive healthcare.', 'Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the argument in Text 1?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "By noting that population-level study identifies risk factors and prevention targets that complement antibiotic treatment."}, {"id": "B", "text": "By arguing that prevention is unrelated to public health."}, {"id": "C", "text": "By claiming that epidemiology studies individual cells only."}, {"id": "D", "text": "By denying that antibiotics treat bacterial infections."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Antibiotic", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antibiotic; Wikipedia, "Epidemiology", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epidemiology', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M37-X017', 'A', ARRAY['A']::TEXT[], 'Text 1 describes antibiotics as agents used to treat and prevent bacterial infections. Text 2 describes epidemiology as studying disease in populations and identifying risk factors and prevention targets, so its author would present that population approach as complementary.', '{"D": "Text 2 does not address antibiotics directly.", "C": "Epidemiology studies populations, not cells only.", "B": "Text 2 calls prevention central to public health."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, external_id, assessments, section, domain, skill, difficulty, format, stimulus, prompt, choices, figure_metadata, source_id, source_name, license, attribution, is_released_practice_set, status) VALUES ('RW-M37-X018', 'HDSAT-RW-M37-X018', ARRAY['SAT', 'PSAT/NMSQT', 'PSAT 10', 'PSAT 8/9']::TEXT[], 'Reading and Writing', 'Craft and Structure', 'Cross-Text Connections', 'Medium', 'multiple_choice', 'Text 1
An antibiotic is a type of antimicrobial substance which is active against bacteria. It is the most important type of antibacterial agent for fighting bacterial infections, and antibiotic medications are widely used in the treatment and prevention of such infections.

Text 2
Epidemiology is the study and analysis of the distribution (who, when, and where), patterns and determinants of health and disease conditions in a defined population, and application of this knowledge to prevent diseases. It is a cornerstone of public health, and shapes policy decisions and evidence-based practice by identifying risk factors for disease and targets for preventive healthcare.', 'Which choice best describes the relationship between the two texts?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "Text 2 focuses on the chemical structure of drugs."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Text 2 argues that antibiotics are ineffective."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Text 1 describes a treatment, while Text 2 describes a population-level approach to preventing disease."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Both texts describe the same laboratory technique."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Antibiotic", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antibiotic; Wikipedia, "Epidemiology", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epidemiology', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M37-X018', 'C', ARRAY['C']::TEXT[], 'Text 1 centers on antibiotics as medicines for bacterial infections. Text 2 centers on epidemiology, the population-level study of disease distribution and determinants used to prevent disease, so the texts describe complementary clinical and public-health approaches.', '{"D": "One text is about medication, the other about populations.", "B": "Text 2 does not evaluate antibiotics.", "A": "Text 2 does not analyze drug chemistry."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, external_id, assessments, section, domain, skill, difficulty, format, stimulus, prompt, choices, figure_metadata, source_id, source_name, license, attribution, is_released_practice_set, status) VALUES ('RW-M37-X019', 'HDSAT-RW-M37-X019', ARRAY['SAT', 'PSAT/NMSQT', 'PSAT 10', 'PSAT 8/9']::TEXT[], 'Reading and Writing', 'Craft and Structure', 'Cross-Text Connections', 'Medium', 'multiple_choice', 'Text 1
Cryptography, or cryptology, is the practice and study of techniques for secure communication in the presence of adversarial behavior. More generally, cryptography is about constructing and analyzing protocols that prevent third parties or the public from reading private messages.

Text 2
The Internet (or internet) is the global system of interconnected computer networks that uses the Internet protocol suite (TCP/IP) to communicate between networks and devices. It is a network of networks that comprises private, public, academic, business, and government networks of local to global scope, linked by electronic, wireless, and optical networking technologies.', 'Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the argument in Text 1?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "By noting that the global network described in Text 2 carries the communications that cryptographic protocols are designed to protect."}, {"id": "B", "text": "By denying that the Internet connects networks."}, {"id": "C", "text": "By arguing that the Internet does not use protocols."}, {"id": "D", "text": "By claiming that cryptography only protects paper mail."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Cryptography", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cryptography; Wikipedia, "Internet", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M37-X019', 'A', ARRAY['A']::TEXT[], 'Text 1 describes cryptography as techniques and protocols that keep third parties from reading private messages. Text 2 describes the Internet as a global network of networks that communicates data, so its author would identify that network as a setting where such protection is needed.', '{"B": "Text 2 defines the Internet as interconnected networks.", "D": "Text 1 is about digital secure communication.", "C": "Text 2 says the Internet uses TCP/IP."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
