The Internet (or internet) is the global system of interconnected computer networks that uses the Internet protocol suite (TCP/IP) to communicate between networks and devices. It is a network of networks that comprises private, public, academic, business, and government networks of local to global scope, linked by electronic, wireless, and optical networking technologies.', 'Which choice best describes the relationship between the two texts?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "Text 2 argues that cryptography is obsolete."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Text 2 describes the history of encryption only."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Text 1 describes how the Internet was built."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Text 1 describes techniques for securing communication, and Text 2 describes the network infrastructure those techniques can protect."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Cryptography", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cryptography; Wikipedia, "Internet", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
